xnu 0508: create a directory over the USB command channel

`wfile` can replace or create a file, but not a directory, and installing a
driver bundle needs one: `/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL` exists in the image and
is writable at runtime, while the bundle below it is not. The hook runs as the
user and cannot create a root-owned directory, so the kernel does it.

The command is `mkdir PATH`, answered with `mkdir <errno>`. It reuses the
`mondrian_root_mkdir()` helper the HFS bring-up already had (namei with
OP_MKDIR and LOCKPARENT, VATTR type VDIR, vn_authorize_mkdir then VNOP_MKDIR),
which until now was static and only created `/private/var/vm` at boot; it is
now exported. The mode is 0755, the owner root, and an existing directory
answers EEXIST, so a repeated install is harmless.

The host side is `tools/usb-ring.py mkdir PATH`. Together with `wfile` it
installs the speaker HAL bundle without reflashing the root image:

  python tools/usb-ring.py mkdir /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/MondrianAudio.driver
  python tools/usb-ring.py wfile /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/MondrianAudio.driver/Info.plist Info.plist
  python tools/usb-ring.py wfile /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/MondrianAudio.driver/MondrianAudio MondrianAudio

which is what `tools/install-mondrian-hal.sh` runs.
